1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,960
I'm the only Palestinian American serving in Congress, Mr. Chair, and my perspective is needed here now more than ever.

2
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:10,660
I will not be silenced, and I will not let you distort my words.

3
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:19,200
Folks forget I'm from the city of Detroit, the most beautiful blackest city in the country where I learned to speak truth to power even if my voice shakes.

4
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:27,360
Trying to bully or censor me won't work, because this movement for a ceasefire is much bigger than one person.

5
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,640
It's growing every single day.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:41,160
There are millions of people across our country who oppose Netanyahu's extremism and are done watching our government support collective punishment and the use of white phosphorus bombs that melt flesh to the bone.

7
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:49,360
They are done watching our government, Mr. Chair, supporting cutting off food, water, electricity, and medical care to millions of people with nowhere to go.

8
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:54,600
Like me, Mr. Chair, they don't believe the answer to war crimes is more war crimes.

9
00:00:54,600 --> 00:01:00,400
The refusal of Congress and the administration to acknowledge Palestinian lives is chipping away at my soul.

10
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:03,300
Over 10,000 Palestinians have been killed.

11
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:05,500
Majority, majority were children.

12
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:08,100
But let me be clear.

13
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:13,460
My criticism has always been of the Israeli government and Netanyahu's actions.

14
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:16,700
It is important to separate people and governments, Mr. Chair.

15
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:18,700
No government is beyond criticism.

16
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:29,660
The idea that criticizing the government of Israel is anti-Semitic sets a very dangerous precedent, and it's being used to silence diverse voices speaking up for human rights across our nation.

17
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:38,520
Do you realize what it's like, Mr. Chair, for the people outside the chamber right now listening in agony to their own government dehumanizing them?

18
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:46,520
To hear the President of the United States we helped elect dispute death tolls as we see video after video of dead children and parents under rubble?

19
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:54,320
Mr. Chair, do you know what it's like to fear rising hate crimes, to know how Islamophobia and anti-Semitism makes us all less safe,

20
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:59,380
and worry that your own child might suffer the horrors that your six-year-old Wadiat did in Illinois?

21
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:05,480
I can't believe I have to say this, but Palestinian people are not disposable.

22
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:27,250
We are human beings, just like anyone else.

23
00:02:28,090 --> 00:02:38,690
My city, my grandmother, like all Palestinians, just wants to live her life with freedom and human dignity we all deserve.

24
00:02:38,690 --> 00:02:46,390
Speaking up to save lives, Mr. Chair, no matter faith, no matter ethnicity, should not be controversial in this chamber.

25
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:52,150
The cries of the Palestinian and Israeli children sound no different to me.

26
00:02:52,930 --> 00:03:00,330
Why what I don't understand is why the cries of Palestinians sound different to you all.

27
00:03:01,630 --> 00:03:04,450
We cannot lose our shared humanity, Mr. Chair.

28
00:03:04,450 --> 00:03:12,690
I hear the voices of advocates in Israel, in Palestine, across America and around the world for peace.

29
00:03:13,150 --> 00:03:22,290
I am inspired by the courageous survivors in Israel who have lost loved ones, yet are calling for a ceasefire and the end to violence.

30
00:03:22,290 --> 00:03:30,550
I am grateful to the people in the streets for the peace movement, with countless Jewish Americans across the country,

31
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:35,230
standing up and lovingly saying, not in our name.

32
00:03:35,230 --> 00:03:42,210
We will continue to call for a ceasefire, Mr. Chair, for the immediate delivery of critical humanitarian aid to Gaza,

33
00:03:42,470 --> 00:03:47,830
for the release of all hostages and those arbitrarily detained, and for every American to come home.

34
00:03:48,310 --> 00:03:54,230
We will continue to work for a real lasting peace that upholds human rights and dignity of all people,

35
00:03:54,750 --> 00:03:57,970
and centers in peaceful coexistence between Israelis and Palestinians,

36
00:03:57,970 --> 00:04:06,290
and censures no one, not no one, and ensures that no person, no child, has to suffer or live in fear of violence.

37
00:04:07,090 --> 00:04:10,810
71% of Michigan Democrats support a ceasefire.

38
00:04:11,370 --> 00:04:15,590
So you can try to censor me, but you can't silence their voices.

39
00:04:16,330 --> 00:04:23,010
I urge my colleagues to join with the majority of Americans and support a ceasefire now to save as many lives as possible.

40
00:04:23,010 --> 00:04:28,530
President Biden must listen to and represent all of us, not just some of us.

41
00:04:29,210 --> 00:04:34,470
I urge the president to have the courage to call for a ceasefire and the end of killings.

42
00:04:34,810 --> 00:04:35,590
Thank you, and I yield.

